  "evidence": [
    {
      "sourceId": "src-80a5e1c82d31d5aa",
      "quote": "Neonatal Health Services Research Lab The Neonatal Health Services Research Lab seeks to improve the quality of care for mothers and newborns, particularly among preterm infants. Our Research Our particular research interests include perinatal and neonatal epidemiology, simulation in neonatal resuscitation, and benefits of breastmilk for preterm infants. We also conduct quality improvement efforts and seek to disseminate and implement evidence-based practices. We are interested in studying healthcare delivery for neonates using a variety of research methods ranging from qualitative studies to large population-based analyses. A focus of our research is on health disparities and methods to improve outcomes for hospitalized neonates and their families. About Research Publications News Team Gallery Contact Us",
